## Implementation Steps

1. Create `data/intelligence/search-templates.json`:
   ```json
   {
     "micro-saas": {
       "instance_search": [
         {"query": "site:microacquire.com SaaS under $5000 revenue", "purpose": "find_real_listings"},
         {"query": "site:reddit.com/r/SaaS 'MRR' OR '$' micro SaaS {year}", "purpose": "find_income_reports"},
         {"query": "indie hackers micro SaaS revenue report {year}", "purpose": "find_public_metrics"}
       ],
       "validation": [
         {"query": "{specific_product} reviews users", "purpose": "demand_signal"},
         {"query": "{specific_niche} SaaS free alternative open source", "purpose": "moat_check"}
       ],
       "anti_confirmation": [
         {"query": "micro SaaS failure rate statistics {year}", "purpose": "base_rate"},
         {"query": "why micro SaaS fails common mistakes", "purpose": "failure_archaeology"}
       ]
     },
     "digital-template-library": { ... },
     ...
   }
   ```

2. Populate templates for all 15+ asset classes. Per class, minimum:
   - 3 instance_search queries (find real sellers/products)
   - 2 validation queries (verify demand + check moat)
   - 2 anti_confirmation queries (failure rate + failure patterns)

3. Create `search-rewriter.py` with:
   - `load_templates()` — loads search-templates.json
   - `expand_template(query_str, context)` — replaces {year}, {niche}, {platform}, {specific_product} with actual values from portfolio context
   - `rewrite_searches(portfolio_output, context)` — main function
     - For each asset class in portfolio allocations
     - Load that class's templates
     - Expand with context variables
     - Return structured query plan

4. Context variables auto-populated:
   - `{year}` = current year (2026)
   - `{niche}` = from founder profile or "general" default
   - `{platform}` = primary platform for that asset class (Gumroad, Etsy, etc.)
   - `{specific_product}` = placeholder for instance-level drilldown (filled later by LLM during research)

5. Output format:
   ```json
   {
     "query_plan": [
       {
         "asset_class": "digital-template-library",
         "allocation_usd": 100,
         "queries": {
           "instance_search": ["site:gumroad.com notion template revenue 2026", ...],
           "validation": [...],
           "anti_confirmation": [...]
         },
         "total_queries": 7,
         "priority": "HIGH"
       }
     ],
     "total_queries": 21,
     "generic_queries_replaced": ["business ideas $500 capital", "micro business profitable 2026"]
   }
   ```

6. Wire CLI: `--portfolio-json` or `--portfolio-file` input, JSON output

## Success Criteria

- [ ] `search-templates.json` has templates for all 15+ asset classes
- [ ] Each class has >= 7 queries (3 instance + 2 validation + 2 anti-confirmation)
- [ ] Template expansion replaces all {variables} correctly
- [ ] Output includes total_queries count and priority ranking
- [ ] No generic "business ideas" queries in output — all asset-class-specific

## Risk Assessment

| Risk | Mitigation |
|------|------------|
| Templates go stale (platforms change) | Year variable auto-updated; templates structured for easy edit |
| Too many queries slows pipeline | Priority ranking ensures top classes get searched first; query budget cap configurable |
| Some queries return no results | Fallback: if instance_search returns <3 results, widen to category-level search |
